    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #85 Quantitative Review & Parameter Mutation\nCycle #85 demonstrated strong directional alpha in Out-of-Sample testing (53.3% Win Rate, 0.96 Profit Factor, +\u20b949.67 Gross P&L), coming within \u20b94.59 of net profitability despite \u20b954.26 in fee drag. Forensic analysis of the 7 losing trades revealed two primary failure modes: mid-morning (10:25\u201311:25 IST) liquidity sweep false positives that immediately reversed into 0.65% stops (e.g., TATASTEEL, NTPC), and low-volatility afternoon stagnation leading to fee-negative EOD/breakeven exits (ITC, ICICIBANK). To push the Profit Factor comfortably above 1.15, we are tightening `min_sl_pct` to `0.55%` to truncate adverse excursion losses, raising `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to `2.80x` to demand institutional-grade participation before entry, expanding `min_target_pct` to `1.35%` to maximize reward-to-fee ratios, and pulling `breakeven_trigger_r` down to `1.00R` to neutralize downside risk faster on stalling momentum."
